[E-TYPE-MISMATCH] Error: type mismatch
    ╭─[ reject/match-equation-leaves-solution.sw:14:15 ]
    │
 13 │   match field: slot.field with
    │                ─────┬────  
    │                     ╰────── the `match`'s scrutinee, still in this type
 14 │     | None => lem slot
    │               ────┬───  
    │                   ╰───── expected `Q None 3 4`, but this has type `Q slot.field (?0 slot field) 5`
    │ 
    │ Note 1: `?0` is the implicit argument `n` of `lem`, which wasn't worked out from the other arguments or the expected type; give it with `[n := …]`
    │ 
    │ Note 2: a term written out inside a branch (an explicit argument, or a type you wrote) isn't refined by the `match`: only the goal and the variables in scope are, so it still has the scrutinee in it. Write `_` for such an argument, so it is inferred from the hypothesis (docs/syntax.md, "Proving things about a definition with an inner `match`")
